-- title:
--   Local blow-up chart of a Drinfeld chart presentation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a commutative local ring $A$ with algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$, and elements $\varpi,\varpi_t \in A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$. Let $W_1$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain) and $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, with $\sigma_1$ surjective modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ and $\sigma_1^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{W_1}) = \mathfrak m_A$. Let $f_1,u_1,v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, assume $\sigma_1\varpi_t \ne 0$, and put $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$ with reduction map $\mathrm{mk}_S$, assuming the class of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$ is a non-zero-divisor in $S$; assume also that $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ acts on the residue field $\kappa_A$ by an algebra structure. Set $L_{\mathrm{loc}} = S[1/\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)]$ with structure map $\iota_S$, let $x_i$ be the image of $X_i$ times the inverse of $\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, and let $R_{\mathrm{loc}} \subseteq L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ be the subring generated by $\iota_S(S)$ together with $x_0,x_1$. The assertion is that $\iota_S(S) \subseteq R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, that $x_0,x_1 \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, and that there are a ring homomorphism $t_W : W_1 \to \kappa_A$, an element $c_R \in \kappa_A$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho_R : R_{\mathrm{loc}} \to \mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_A = \kappa_A[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ such that $t_W \circ \sigma_1$ is the residue map of $A$, $t_W$ vanishes on $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, $c_R \ne 0$, $\rho_R(\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S F))$ is the image of $t_W$ of the constant coefficient of $F$ for every power series $F$, $\rho_R(x_0) = c_R\,x$ and $\rho_R(x_1) = c_R\,y$ for the classes $x,y$ of $X_0,X_1$, $\rho_R$ is surjective, and $\rho_R(r) = 0$ exactly when $r$ lies in the ideal of $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ generated by $\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi))$.
--
--   This identifies the special fibre of the blow-up chart obtained by dividing the two formal coordinates by $\sigma_1\varpi_t$ at a supersingular-type point of an auxiliary-level modular curve: the chart ring maps onto the affine Drinfeld curve over the residue field, with kernel generated by the uniformiser. It is the $W_1$-side input to the assembly statements [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat_of_dvd), and is obtained from the corresponding statement for an abstract chart presentation over a discrete valuation ring together with the integrality of the Drinfeld coordinate ring.
